ll measure over and  over and over again and we'll compare  other results too and so I measure water  and I needed water from a really hot  place and from a really cold place um so  I ended up buying two cases of bottled  water one from a high elevation site in  Colorado and one from Hawaii so I had to  basically justify spending forty dollars  on fancy bottles of water from that you  can't drink yeah that I that I'm  actually never tasted oh and then once  those bottles of water arrived I had to  I can just store them in plastic bottles  because they might evaporate and that  would throw off what I'm trying to  measure and so I needed really good  containers to pour all the bottles of  water into and it turns out that the  type of containers I needed were beer  kegs so in the space of a week I ordered  forty dollars worth of bottled water and  three beer kegs so did you did you  justify beer kegs work for science they  were for sign when we had to specially  modify them so that we could do exactly  what we wanted to do with them that's  removing okay so thank you so much for  participating in this Google hangout I'm  very excited to be able to post this on  Eureka lab thank you so much for your  time and I hope that you inspire lots of  people to go a look at their livers in a  new way thanks for having me
 

